cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to these instances, please cite them as below."
title: "Small MMS counterexamples: 5 agents / 13 goods and 4 agents / 11 goods"
abstract: >-
  Instances of fair division with additive positive integer valuations in which
  no allocation gives every agent her maximin share. The 5-agent, 13-good
  instance has MMS 29 with best achievable minimum 28, giving the upper bound
  alpha <= 28/29 on the largest alpha for which alpha-MMS allocations always
  exist (any number of agents), improving 39/40 from the 3-agent, 9-good
  instance of Feige, Sapir and Tauber (WINE 2021), and alpha_5 <= 28/29 for five
  agents (previously 1 - 1/5^4 = 624/625). The 4-agent, 11-good instance has MMS
  30 with best achievable minimum 29, giving alpha_4 <= 29/30 (previously
  67/68); eleven goods is minimal for four agents, by Hummel (IJCAI 2023).
  Established by exhaustive enumeration, reproduced by independent programs of
  different design (literal enumeration and subset dynamic programming), with
  compact per-instance certificates that can be checked by hand.
authors:
  - family-names: Alexandrov
    given-names: Andrey
    email: alexandrov.home@gmail.com
date-released: 2026-09-01
version: "1.2"
repository-code: "https://github.com/andrewchatgptkz-ops/mms4-small-counterexamples"
